#
# Conformance case: transaction/hypothetical-isolation.
#
# The SAME serial-conjunction transaction program (φ ⊗ ψ over s0 → s1 → s2) is run, but
# its transaction-program root is bound — IN THE WORLD FACTS (input.nq) — to a governing
# logic:ReasoningContract whose logic:executionMode is logic:HypotheticalExecution. The
# sandbox operator is a SEPARATE, orthogonal facet (logic:ExecutionMode: commit vs.
# discard), NOT modal possibility (◇). The verdict is computed identically to a committed
# run, but the emission differs: the engine records the logic:TransactionOutcome with its
# verdict plus a SINGLE content-addressed logic:executedHypotheticallyAs witness, and
# SUPPRESSES the effect substrate entirely — no logic:Path, no per-step logic:TransactionStep,
# no supersession quads. Suppression-never-erasure holds for free: the discarded effects are
# never asserted, so the start state is untouched and the witness is the sole standing trace.
# Proves the hypothetical (sandbox) isolation contract at the corpus level.
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom the
# projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live in
# input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/transaction/hypothetical-isolation/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .

# The compile-time reasoning contract selects the Evolution facet that classifies this
# transaction program. logic:TransactionPathEvolution drives certification to the
# transaction-path decidability class (conflict-serializability; PTIME classification,
# not search). The contract also declares logic:executionMode logic:HypotheticalExecution
# for fidelity with the world-facts wiring that actually drives the sandbox emission.
ex:TransactionContract a logic:ReasoningContract ;
    logic:evolution logic:TransactionPathEvolution ;
    logic:executionMode logic:HypotheticalExecution .
